1
00:00:00,033 --> 00:00:05,005
Don't get involved in Hans' investigation.

2
00:00:05,005 --> 00:00:07,132
Tell him to stop.

3
00:00:07,133 --> 00:00:08,735
No, wait.

4
00:00:08,735 --> 00:00:10,203
- Come on, let's go.
- I will protect her.

5
00:00:10,203 --> 00:00:12,372
My dad saw the man in this video.

6
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:15,183
- And he knows him.
- It will make my investigation easier.

7
00:00:15,183 --> 00:00:17,677
- Come on, let's see him.
- You can't talk to him, Hans.

8
00:00:17,677 --> 00:00:20,613
Sometimes, people lack courage.

9
00:00:20,613 --> 00:00:23,042
Courage to face their problem.

10
00:00:23,042 --> 00:00:25,660
Sometimes,
the solution is right in front of us.

11
00:00:25,660 --> 00:00:27,787
But we are dominated by fear.

12
00:00:27,787 --> 00:00:29,222
Are you going to kill me?

13
00:00:29,222 --> 00:00:33,993
If you were my target,
you wouldn't be able to talk anymore.

14
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:35,558
Is it because of this?

15
00:00:35,558 --> 00:00:38,261
Do you think Liam and Joyce have an affair?

16
00:00:38,261 --> 00:00:40,633
It's just a film.

17
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:44,488
My daughter and I are not
the kind of people you can fool.

18
00:00:44,488 --> 00:00:45,511
Hello.

19
00:00:45,511 --> 00:00:46,639
Hello, everyone.

20
00:00:46,639 --> 00:00:49,909
Really? Maxine?

21
00:00:49,909 --> 00:00:51,044
Joyce.

22
00:00:51,044 --> 00:00:52,378
Maxine.

23
00:00:52,378 --> 00:00:55,281
You know we have a problem, Liam.

24
00:00:55,281 --> 00:00:56,334
Can you tell me the truth?

25
00:00:56,334 --> 00:00:57,501
Are you just staying with me

26
00:00:57,501 --> 00:01:01,100
because you know
my dad might do something if we break up?

27
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,133
I don't know anymore!

28
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:03,935
I don't know! I'm confused!

29
00:01:03,935 --> 00:01:05,703
I just want to explode!

30
00:01:05,704 --> 00:01:08,469
Sorry if you feel alone.

31
00:01:11,934 --> 00:01:14,103
This is what I only got.

32
00:01:14,103 --> 00:01:19,174
I'm sorry
if I dragged you into my miserable life.

33
00:01:53,267 --> 00:01:56,670
<i>I want to explode
because this is already so full.</i>

34
00:01:56,670 --> 00:01:59,540
<i>This is full of things I never wanted.</i>

35
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:02,376
<i>Like our relationship?</i>

36
00:02:02,376 --> 00:02:05,012
<i>But I don't think...</i>

37
00:02:05,012 --> 00:02:09,015
<i>I'm the right person to make you feel that.</i>

38
00:02:17,346 --> 00:02:19,601
Hans, where are you?

39
00:02:19,601 --> 00:02:21,810
Please talk to me.

40
00:02:30,990 --> 00:02:32,544
Hans.

41
00:02:38,644 --> 00:02:42,427
Joyce.

42
00:02:42,427 --> 00:02:46,253
<i>Love, can you give us privacy for now?</i>

43
00:02:46,253 --> 00:02:48,122
I'll give Savana a sponge bath.

44
00:02:48,122 --> 00:02:50,309
- Surprise.
- What are you doing here?

45
00:02:50,309 --> 00:02:52,777
I just thought I'd surprise you.

46
00:02:55,229 --> 00:02:57,598
Joyce.

47
00:02:57,598 --> 00:02:58,765
Dad.

48
00:02:58,765 --> 00:03:01,101
- Dad, what are you doing here?
- You're so beautiful.

49
00:03:01,101 --> 00:03:03,604
How did you get out of the center, Dad?

50
00:03:03,604 --> 00:03:05,772
I'll explain later.

51
00:03:05,772 --> 00:03:09,476
My dear, I need to talk to Hans.

52
00:03:09,476 --> 00:03:11,577
Do you know where he is?

53
00:03:13,303 --> 00:03:17,284
I have vital information
regarding his investigation.

54
00:03:17,284 --> 00:03:20,687
Dad, you won't be able to talk to Hans.

55
00:03:20,687 --> 00:03:24,680
- Why?
- I also have something to explain to him.

56
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,460
This is important.

57
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:28,962
This is more important.

58
00:03:28,962 --> 00:03:32,765
Okay, Dad. You can tell me.

59
00:03:36,637 --> 00:03:43,477
The man in the CCTV footage
we watched on Hans' phone...

60
00:03:43,477 --> 00:03:46,245
The murder suspect in the death

61
00:03:46,245 --> 00:03:49,963
of a constructor worker in Casa Fuerte...

62
00:03:51,018 --> 00:03:54,584
That man's name is Lando.

63
00:03:55,989 --> 00:03:59,927
And that demon only works for one man.

64
00:04:02,831 --> 00:04:04,699
What are you saying?

65
00:04:04,699 --> 00:04:09,370
There's someone else behind the murder?

66
00:04:10,605 --> 00:04:13,675
It's Congressman Ramon dela Peña.

67
00:04:13,675 --> 00:04:15,910
Lando is his right-hand man.

68
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:20,214
He does Ramon's dirty job.

69
00:04:21,616 --> 00:04:25,046
How did you know all that?

70
00:04:26,287 --> 00:04:29,390
I used to work for Ramon, too.

71
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:34,929
I regretted and paid for it.

72
00:04:35,597 --> 00:04:39,934
When Ramon almost got caught,
Lando forced me.

73
00:04:39,934 --> 00:04:47,509
They forced me to take the blame.

74
00:04:47,509 --> 00:04:50,879
I became their scapegoat.

75
00:04:50,879 --> 00:04:52,914
And I couldn't say no.

76
00:04:52,914 --> 00:04:56,651
Because they told me...

77
00:04:56,651 --> 00:05:01,289
they warned me that you would get hurt

78
00:05:01,289 --> 00:05:03,724
if I didn't do what they wanted.

79
00:05:05,460 --> 00:05:08,062
I will never let that happen.

80
00:05:09,314 --> 00:05:12,467
They are evil.

81
00:05:12,467 --> 00:05:15,270
Ramon and Lando.

82
00:05:15,270 --> 00:05:18,173
And if I speak up, who will believe me?

83
00:05:18,173 --> 00:05:23,544
Who will listen to
a junkie and an ex-convict?

84
00:05:24,379 --> 00:05:26,280
Who am I to speak up?

85
00:05:31,572 --> 00:05:35,508
Dad, are they the reason
you got separated from me?

86
00:05:40,581 --> 00:05:44,150
Is he the reason your life got ruined?

87
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,836
We need to be careful, dear.

88
00:05:48,836 --> 00:05:51,171
We need to be careful.

89
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,808
Don't worry, Dad.

90
00:05:56,010 --> 00:05:58,746
We'll not be scared of them.

91
00:05:59,981 --> 00:06:05,320
This is the perfect time
to use my position and influence

92
00:06:05,320 --> 00:06:07,821
and fight for what's right.

93
00:06:10,024 --> 00:06:12,269
People will listen to me.

94
00:06:12,269 --> 00:06:16,497
We will expose how evil Congressman Ramon is.

95
00:06:39,654 --> 00:06:41,455
Dad...

96
00:06:44,158 --> 00:06:46,360
There's something you need to know.

97
00:06:52,749 --> 00:06:56,371
Stay here for now, Dad.

98
00:06:56,371 --> 00:06:58,439
I'll just let them know I'm leaving.

99
00:07:33,775 --> 00:07:36,110
Liam...

100
00:07:36,110 --> 00:07:37,478
Joyce.

101
00:07:37,478 --> 00:07:41,883
Liam, I... I need to go.

102
00:07:41,883 --> 00:07:44,551
I need to talk to Hans.

103
00:07:46,285 --> 00:07:49,087
Is this because of what I told you earlier?

104
00:07:50,574 --> 00:07:53,977
This is more important than that.

105
00:07:55,829 --> 00:07:57,464
Joyce, I'm sorry.

106
00:07:57,464 --> 00:07:58,732
I'm sorry for all...

107
00:07:58,732 --> 00:08:00,734
Liam, please. You have to let me go.

108
00:08:00,734 --> 00:08:02,535
Please.

109
00:08:03,871 --> 00:08:06,172
Joyce, are you okay?

110
00:08:07,141 --> 00:08:08,976
Let's shoot this last scene.

111
00:08:08,976 --> 00:08:10,844
So we can close the sequence.

112
00:08:10,844 --> 00:08:13,396
I need to go.

113
00:08:14,568 --> 00:08:16,417
I knew it.

114
00:08:16,417 --> 00:08:19,018
She has something against me again.

115
00:08:20,921 --> 00:08:23,389
Maxine, no...

116
00:08:29,229 --> 00:08:33,200
Guys, let's pack up for now.

117
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,768
- What did he say?
- What?

118
00:08:34,768 --> 00:08:36,069
- He said we'll pack up.
- Director Phil.

119
00:08:36,069 --> 00:08:38,839
Maxine, I'm sorry, but we'll pack up for now.

120
00:08:38,839 --> 00:08:40,374
Josh, I'm sorry.

121
00:08:40,374 --> 00:08:42,242
What are we going to do?

122
00:08:42,242 --> 00:08:44,877
- Okay, okay.
- What about clustering?

123
00:08:48,849 --> 00:08:53,249
Check the clustering.

124
00:09:16,376 --> 00:09:18,084
Director Phil...

125
00:09:20,342 --> 00:09:23,773
Okay, let's do it.

126
00:09:23,773 --> 00:09:26,853
It's just one sequence, anyway.

127
00:09:28,455 --> 00:09:32,425
Joyce... Joyce, are you sure?

128
00:09:36,463 --> 00:09:38,170
Yes.

129
00:09:40,100 --> 00:09:42,302
Let's finish it.

130
00:09:44,866 --> 00:09:47,508
Okay, let's resume.

131
00:09:47,508 --> 00:09:49,176
- Okay, let's fix it.
- Wardrobe!

132
00:09:49,176 --> 00:09:50,944
Is this Joyce's outfit for the scene?

133
00:09:50,944 --> 00:09:53,480
- She needs to change.
- Double time! Hurry up!

134
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:54,914
Noted, Sir.

135
00:09:55,983 --> 00:09:58,852
Okay, we have two cameras here.

136
00:09:58,852 --> 00:09:59,920
Okay?

137
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:01,622
Maxine...

138
00:10:01,622 --> 00:10:05,370
There. Your arm is locked on Joyce's neck.

139
00:10:05,372 --> 00:10:06,839
And there's a gun on the other hand.

140
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,600
It's pointed at her temple.

141
00:10:08,601 --> 00:10:11,891
You'll say your last line
in this scene, okay?

142
00:10:11,891 --> 00:10:15,135
The line that says,
"You left Chito, and I took care of him".

143
00:10:15,135 --> 00:10:15,801
Okay?

144
00:10:15,801 --> 00:10:18,939
And, then, at that part,
you'll have your realization.

145
00:10:18,939 --> 00:10:20,507
- They're intense, right?
- Yes.

146
00:10:20,507 --> 00:10:26,579
So you'll beg her to let go of Joyce.

147
00:10:26,579 --> 00:10:31,842
While he's begging,
you will have a change of heart.

148
00:10:31,842 --> 00:10:34,388
And while she's faltering,

149
00:10:34,388 --> 00:10:37,124
you'll now have an opportunity, Joyce...

150
00:10:37,124 --> 00:10:39,526
An opportunity to escape.

151
00:10:39,526 --> 00:10:42,195
When you escape towards here... There.

152
00:10:42,195 --> 00:10:45,699
We'll edit your escape in slow motion.

153
00:10:45,699 --> 00:10:47,167
And when you escape...

154
00:10:47,167 --> 00:10:50,137
We need to see it in your face...

155
00:10:50,137 --> 00:10:52,639
We'll focus the camera on you...
on your face.

156
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:54,274
Your face must show the line that says,

157
00:10:54,274 --> 00:10:57,811
"You and Chito will never be happy".

158
00:10:57,811 --> 00:10:58,734
Okay?

159
00:10:58,734 --> 00:11:02,193
And while she's running, you'll call her.

160
00:11:02,194 --> 00:11:03,687
- Go!
- Cindy!

161
00:11:03,689 --> 00:11:05,481
Cindy! When she turns around...

162
00:11:05,483 --> 00:11:06,705
Bang!

163
00:11:06,707 --> 00:11:08,765
That's it. And then fall.

164
00:11:08,767 --> 00:11:09,663
Fall in his arms.

165
00:11:09,665 --> 00:11:10,816
There.

166
00:11:10,818 --> 00:11:14,834
And you go down slowly, slow down, there.

167
00:11:14,836 --> 00:11:17,331
And then, there's the blood squib.

168
00:11:17,331 --> 00:11:18,398
There's blood there.

169
00:11:18,398 --> 00:11:20,334
It will come out.

170
00:11:20,334 --> 00:11:22,903
And that's it. Okay?

171
00:11:22,903 --> 00:11:24,605
The scene is very intense.

172
00:11:24,605 --> 00:11:26,506
Does everybody understand?

173
00:11:26,506 --> 00:11:28,175
That's what's going to happen.

174
00:11:28,175 --> 00:11:32,412
Everything should be precise
and at the right time.

175
00:11:32,412 --> 00:11:35,515
All of it. Okay?

176
00:11:35,515 --> 00:11:37,484
Where's the prop gun?

177
00:11:37,484 --> 00:11:38,952
The one we prepared earlier?

178
00:11:38,952 --> 00:11:40,968
Yes, Director Phil. Here it is.

179
00:11:40,968 --> 00:11:41,712
[Gun Props]

180
00:11:41,713 --> 00:11:43,853
Come on. Bring it here.

181
00:11:46,573 --> 00:11:48,600
Go, give it to her.

182
00:11:49,442 --> 00:11:51,043
Okay.

183
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,732
Is this a real gun?

184
00:11:52,733 --> 00:11:55,656
Yes, but it only has blank bullets.

185
00:11:55,657 --> 00:11:56,870
Yes.

186
00:11:56,870 --> 00:12:01,085
That's better,
so you can really feel the scene, okay?

187
00:12:01,087 --> 00:12:03,650
It only has a blank bullet.

188
00:12:03,652 --> 00:12:06,780
When you shoot Joyce, it won't reach her.

189
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:12,552
So that is very safe and looks better, okay?

190
00:12:12,552 --> 00:12:15,556
Come on, let's take this.

191
00:12:24,931 --> 00:12:27,266
I want to make it clear.

192
00:12:28,335 --> 00:12:33,240
I want Dad to be prepared if Joyce speaks up.

193
00:12:33,240 --> 00:12:36,276
But I didn't know he'd tell you to come here.

194
00:12:36,276 --> 00:12:40,847
It's too late to regret telling your dad, Via.

195
00:12:40,847 --> 00:12:44,884
Now, what do you want me to do
with Joyce's dad?

196
00:12:46,301 --> 00:12:48,435
Leave him out of this.

197
00:12:52,322 --> 00:12:55,057
No one will believe him anyway.

198
00:12:56,430 --> 00:12:58,297
I'll deal with him.

199
00:13:01,668 --> 00:13:05,005
<i>I thought we'd fight only because of Liam.</i>

200
00:13:05,005 --> 00:13:09,476
<i>Now it's your dad against mine.</i>

201
00:13:09,476 --> 00:13:12,012
<i>Sorry, Joyce.</i>

202
00:13:12,012 --> 00:13:14,981
<i>You've been taking a lot from me.</i>

203
00:13:17,517 --> 00:13:20,120
Hey! Concentrate, everyone! Quiet!

204
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,188
Let's watch this.

205
00:13:27,347 --> 00:13:29,996
I'm begging you.

206
00:13:29,996 --> 00:13:32,132
I didn't mean to hurt you.

207
00:13:32,132 --> 00:13:35,035
Shut up!

208
00:13:35,035 --> 00:13:37,253
Shut up!

209
00:13:41,842 --> 00:13:44,911
You left Chito.

210
00:13:44,911 --> 00:13:47,180
And I took care of him, Cindy.

211
00:13:47,180 --> 00:13:49,182
I did!

212
00:13:49,182 --> 00:13:53,353
Sofia... I'm begging you, put that down!

213
00:13:53,353 --> 00:13:56,316
Cindy has nothing to do with this!

214
00:13:57,591 --> 00:14:00,226
Did you just use me, Chito?

215
00:14:02,028 --> 00:14:03,530
You only fooled me?

216
00:14:03,530 --> 00:14:05,386
That's not true.

217
00:14:20,927 --> 00:14:26,218
Chito, I love you so much.

218
00:14:26,219 --> 00:14:28,088
And I can't bear losing you.

219
00:14:28,088 --> 00:14:30,256
So please, don't leave me.

220
00:14:34,326 --> 00:14:36,094
Cindy!

221
00:15:01,101 --> 00:15:02,642
Sofia.

222
00:15:10,263 --> 00:15:13,566
Cindy!

223
00:15:19,773 --> 00:15:23,643
Cindy!

224
00:15:31,898 --> 00:15:33,033
Cut!

225
00:15:33,035 --> 00:15:34,287
Good take.

226
00:15:34,287 --> 00:15:37,167
Lovely. Perfect!

227
00:15:43,601 --> 00:15:46,098
Joyce, get up.

228
00:15:46,098 --> 00:15:48,514
Joyce, we're done, Joyce. It's a good take.

229
00:15:48,514 --> 00:15:51,271
Joyce, we had a good take.
I'll take care of everything here.

230
00:15:51,271 --> 00:15:53,239
You can go home.

231
00:15:54,580 --> 00:15:56,084
Joyce.

232
00:15:57,944 --> 00:15:59,845
Joyce, get up.

233
00:16:01,014 --> 00:16:05,952
Joyce... Joyce... get up, Joyce.

234
00:16:05,952 --> 00:16:08,170
Joyce... get up.

235
00:16:08,170 --> 00:16:10,290
Joyce...

236
00:16:10,290 --> 00:16:12,158
Hold on.

237
00:16:12,158 --> 00:16:14,527
This is not fake blood.

238
00:16:14,527 --> 00:16:16,708
Joyce... Joyce... what's going on, Joyce?

239
00:16:16,709 --> 00:16:19,632
Joyce, Joyce!

240
00:16:19,633 --> 00:16:21,679
Call a medic!

241
00:16:21,681 --> 00:16:26,786
Joyce...

242
00:16:26,787 --> 00:16:28,748
What happened?

243
00:16:39,851 --> 00:16:41,521
- Joyce, Joyce.
- What?

244
00:16:41,521 --> 00:16:43,690
What happened here?

245
00:16:43,690 --> 00:16:45,859
What happened to my daughter?

246
00:16:45,859 --> 00:16:47,093
I don't know, Uncle Edmond.

247
00:16:47,093 --> 00:16:49,596
- What happened to my daughter?
- I don't know.

248
00:16:49,596 --> 00:16:51,665
Joyce.

249
00:16:51,665 --> 00:16:53,066
Ambulance!

250
00:16:53,066 --> 00:16:55,001
We need an ambulance!

251
00:16:55,001 --> 00:16:57,586
Call an ambulance! Come on!

252
00:16:58,516 --> 00:17:00,540
Joyce, Joyce.

253
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:02,341
Maxine...

254
00:17:03,910 --> 00:17:05,879
The gun you're holding.

255
00:17:05,879 --> 00:17:09,403
Wait, they told me it's a blank bullet.

256
00:17:10,884 --> 00:17:12,719
Where's the medic?

257
00:17:12,719 --> 00:17:15,422
Where's the medic?

258
00:17:15,422 --> 00:17:17,390
Joyce, Joyce.

259
00:17:17,390 --> 00:17:20,392
Joyce, Joyce, Joyce.

260
00:17:23,376 --> 00:17:25,745
Hang in there, dear.

261
00:17:27,133 --> 00:17:32,615
Hang in there, dear.

262
00:17:39,379 --> 00:17:40,981
What happened?

263
00:17:40,981 --> 00:17:42,582
What happened, Joyce?

264
00:17:42,582 --> 00:17:44,550
What happened?

265
00:17:49,990 --> 00:17:53,908
- Joyce, Joyce.
- Hang in there.

266
00:17:53,908 --> 00:17:55,961
Where's the medic?

267
00:18:00,467 --> 00:18:01,735
Joyce, hang in there.

268
00:18:01,735 --> 00:18:03,203
Don't give up.

269
00:18:03,203 --> 00:18:05,304
Hang in there, okay?

270
00:18:06,039 --> 00:18:07,673
You have to fight.

271
00:18:25,725 --> 00:18:29,929
Joyce... Joyce, we're in the hospital.

272
